# What the release image does not need. The build only reads go.mod, go.sum, cmd and
# internal, so everything else stays out of the build context: a Dockerfile that
# copies fewer files caches better, and a stray database or private key in the
# context is a secret that ends up one COPY away from a published image.
#
# bin/ and deploy/ stay in, because `make complement-image` builds its own image from
# this same context and needs the binary it built and its own entrypoint script.

.git
.github
assets
docs
tests
